+
+pluggable_kbytes
+================
+
+Memory the host may still plug into this guest, through a virtio-mem device,
+in kilobytes: reported by sysinfo(2) and /proc/meminfo as total, free and
+available memory, so that a program that sizes itself by the memory it sees
+sizes itself by what the guest may have, not only by what has been plugged so
+far. The guest's own agent writes how much the host may plug from then on; the
+kernel lowers it as memory is plugged and raises it as memory is unplugged, so
+that reading it gives what may still be plugged, the amount the reports add.
+Nothing in the kernel's own accounting counts it.
 
+The default value is 0.
 
+
 stat_interval
